Error: The following argument was not expected: --bogus-flag
Complete a prompt, printed when done

Usage: wally llm generate [OPTIONS] [prompt]

Arguments:
  prompt                      Prompt to complete (omit to read stdin)

Options:
  -h, --help                  Show help
  -m, --model TEXT            Model to use (downloaded if missing)
      --system-prompt, --system TEXT
                              System prompt
      --lora TEXT             LoRA adapter (.gguf) to attach
      --lora-scale FLOAT      LoRA strength (default 1.0)
      --engine TEXT           Engine to run on (mlx, llamacpp, onnx, sherpa)

Sampling:
      --temperature, --temp FLOAT
                              Sampling temperature (0 = engine default)
      --top-p FLOAT           Keep the smallest token set above this probability
      --top-k INT             Sample from this many highest-probability tokens
      --min-p FLOAT           Drop tokens below this share of the top token
      --repetition-penalty FLOAT
                              Penalize tokens already in the context
      --seed INT              Fix the RNG for a repeatable answer
      --frequency-penalty FLOAT
                              Penalize tokens by how often they appeared
      --presence-penalty FLOAT
                              Penalize tokens that appeared at all
      --stop TEXT ...         Stop at this text (repeat for several)
      --max-output-tokens, --max-tokens INT
                              Cap on generated tokens (default 1024)

Reasoning:
      --reasoning {on,off}    Model thinking phase (default on)
      --show-thinking, --hide-thinking
                              Print thinking tokens on stderr (default on)
      --no-think              Same as --reasoning off

Examples:
  wally llm generate -m qwen3-0.6b "explain tunnelling"
  echo "summarise this" | wally llm generate -m qwen3-0.6b
